        <Options>
            <Main applyHouseholdOperatingConditions="false" applyReducedOperatingConditions="false" atypicalElectricalLoads="false" waterConservation="true" referenceHouse="false" greenerHomesTab="false">
                <Vermiculite code="3">
                    <English>No Vermiculite</English>
                    <French>Pas de Vermiculite</French>
                </Vermiculite>
            </Main>
            <WaterConservation LowFlushToilets="3" LowFlushToiletsUpgrade="0" />
            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>The infiltration test has shown air leakage from the following house components:

-	Windows (2nd floor, seal broken)

-	Receptacles

-	Header joist 

-	Furnace combustion air supply

-	Furnace chimney

During the infiltration test walkthrough, we notice air leakage on the items listed above. Airtightness is very important to achieve energy savings.

</airSeal>
                <mainWalls>We recommend upgrading the insulation level. You are eligible for $2.50/square foot for the addition of R-20+, and $ 3.50/square foot for R-30+. </mainWalls>
                <ceilings>At the time of the audit, the insulation level of the attic was estimated to be R-40. The insulation is composed by 2 layers of 6?????????????????? fiberglass batt insulation with an insulation value of R-20/each. We recommend adding insulation to meet the city of Whitehorse standard of R-60.</ceilings>
                <foundation>Most of the heat loss in a home comes from the basement. We strongly recommend adding insulation on the foundation walls and the header joist (perimeter joist). Insulating the basement will contribute directly to energy savings.  </foundation>
                <windows>We recommend the replacement of the windows by triple pane and Energy Star certified units with Lowe coating and Argon filled.</windows>
                <doors>We recommend the replacement of the wood doors with new energy star certified products.  </doors>
                <VentilationSystem>We recommend the installation of an HRV (Heat Recovery Ventilator) HVI (Home Ventilation Institute) and Energy Star certified, to ensure proper ventilation inside your home.</VentilationSystem>
                <Renewables>For any questions concerning the rebates and the programs about solar energy, please follow the link below to get more information:

https://yukon.ca/en/renewable-energy-rebate#eligible-renewable-systems



</Renewables>
                <AdditionalComments>DEPRUSSIRAZION TEST

The depressurization test performed as shown a high risk of combustion gas spillage. Therefore, we recommend verifying your carbon monoxide detectors regularly.

</AdditionalComments>
            </RURComments>
            <GreenerHomes basementSlabInsulated="false" moistureProofCrawlSpace="false" waterproofing="false" roofingMembrane="false" minR10ContinuousExposedFloors="false" backwaterValve="false" sumpPump="false" smartThermostats="false" remoteCommunities="false" evaluationCost="">
                <Community>N/A</Community>
            </GreenerHomes>
        </Options>
